WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.600
First up, less is more.

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.600
Savings.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.600
Pay attention to what you're spending and cut back where you can.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.600
Track your spending over a couple of months.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.600
You'll probably be surprised where your money is going.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.600
Limit eating out.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.600
All those lattes take out dinners on the Go Protein Chakes.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:18.600
Many people find that they spend a large chunk of their income on eating out.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.600
Set a limit for yourself and stick to it.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.600
You should also try to limit impulse purchases.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.600
They can be a killer for your savings.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.600
But it's just so easy.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.600
It is.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.600
But tapping your way to happiness now may make you stressed in the future.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.600
Think through what you buy.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.600
Make sure you need those new shoes or jeans.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.600
And don't forget all those subscription services.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.600
Are you really watching Netflix Prime and HBO?

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.600
How many shows can you really binge at once?

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.600
You can always pause the subscription and pick it back up when you're ready.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.600
It's all about balance.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.600
Use some money to make you happy now and save some to enjoy later.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.000
Number two.
